Add ENABLE_INA219 flag and expose power state at boot

The INA219 is wired to I2C but not detected yet (no 0x40 on the bus).
While it is absent, the firmware treated the reading as valid-but-zero
volts and the battery failsafe would block arming. The new ENABLE_INA219
flag (default 0, like the other peripherals) keeps the power monitor out
of the failsafe until the module is detected and Vin+/Vin- are wired.

Also prints "[ina] ok=... v=... i=..." at boot so bring-up of the module
is visible on the serial console.

